    title: "Morning update",
    summary: "Morning update Good morning Middle East Eye readers, Here are the latest developments: An Israeli attack on an apartment in Gaza City has killed a senior Palestinian security official alongside his wife and two daughters, aged 13 and 15. According to the interior ministry, the man was identified as the director of the Internal Security Service in northern Gaza, Muhammad Majid Abu al-Awf, 47. This marks the second killing of a security official in Gaza in less than 24 hours, with the previous attack killing director-general of the Internal Security Service, Naim Mohammed Abu Nahl. Iran's First Vice President Mohammad Reza Aref said that Tehran is not concerned about the US naval blockade, the semi-official Tasnim news agency reported. He indicated the country's self-reliance with the increase of cargo clearance through its non-southern borders and added that reserves of strategic goods remain strong. Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) Navy said that two \"offending\" oil tankers on the southern and eastern coasts of the Strait of Hormuz suffered explosions. \"These tankers, believing they were secretly trying to pass through the fake Strait of Hormuz route, were prevented from passing by naval mines, causing a massive explosion and fire,\" it said in a statement. The Saudi-led coalition's spokesperson said in a post on X that it targeted \"operational capabilities\" at Yemen's Hodeidah port. Additionally, Turki al-Maliki added that a number of targets in northern Yemen's Saada and Amran governorates were destroyed. The Saudi-led coalition said it intercepted and destroyed four drones in Ras Tanura, located in Saudi Arabia’s Eastern Province. The coalition's spokesperson Turki al-Maliki indicated that a number of fragments had fallen as a result of the interception, with no casualties reported in the initial assessment. A US poll shows Trump's approval at 37 percent, with strong disapproval over his handling of the Iran war.",
