    id: "7f123112f87c87a6518e",
    cat: "conflitti",
    categories: ["conflitti"],
    title: "More on Israeli strike targeting apartment in Gaza City",
    summary: "More on Israeli strike targeting apartment in Gaza City An Israeli attack on an apartment in Gaza City has killed a senior Palestinian security official alongside his wife and two daughters, aged 13 and 15. According to the Interior Ministry, the man was identified as the director of the Internal Security Service in northern Gaza, Muhammad Majid Abu al-Awf, 47. The ministry slammed the attack as a \"horrific massacre\" and called for \"urgent and genuine action to restrain the occupation from committing further crimes against innocent civilians\" in the Gaza Strip. \"The Ministry of Interior and National Security condemns this heinous crime against security personnel and affirms that it comes within the context of ongoing attempts to undermine the security apparatus in the Gaza Strip in an effort to spread chaos within Palestinian society.\" Earlier, the director-general of the Internal Security Service, Naim Mohammed Abu Nahl, was assassinated in an Israeli strike west of Gaza City.",
    preview: "More on Israeli strike targeting apartment in Gaza City An Israeli attack on an apartment in Gaza City has killed a senior Palestinian security official alongside his wife and two daughters, aged 13 and 15. According to the Interior Ministry, the man was identified as the director of the Internal Security Service in northern Gaza, Muhammad Majid Abu al-Awf, 47.",
    body: "More on Israeli strike targeting apartment in Gaza City An Israeli attack on an apartment in Gaza City has killed a senior Palestinian security official alongside his wife and two daughters, aged 13 and 15. According to the Interior Ministry, the man was identified as the director of the Internal Security Service in northern Gaza, Muhammad Majid Abu al-Awf, 47. The ministry slammed the attack as a \"horrific massacre\" and called for \"urgent and genuine action to restrain the occupation from committing further crimes against innocent civilians\" in the Gaza Strip.\n\n\"The Ministry of Interior and National Security condemns this heinous crime against security personnel and affirms that it comes within the context of ongoing attempts to undermine the security apparatus in the Gaza Strip in an effort to spread chaos within Palestinian society.\" Earlier, the director-general of the Internal Security Service, Naim Mohammed Abu Nahl, was assassinated in an Israeli strike west of Gaza City.",
